Why This Market Matters
Power modules sit at the core of DC EV charging systems and directly influence charging speed, efficiency, reliability, and cabinet design. As charging networks move toward 150 kW-plus systems and higher-voltage vehicle architectures, demand for scalable power-conversion blocks is increasing. Modular architectures allow charging operators and equipment manufacturers to add or replace individual modules rather than redesign complete systems. The adoption of SiC semiconductors, advanced thermal management, remote diagnostics, and bidirectional power capabilities is also creating opportunities for differentiated products.

